    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EExisting trees \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Ebe retained and removal \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Eonly be considered where it can be clearly demonstrated that the design cannot reasonably be altered to allow their retention. Where removal is unavoidable, replacement planting \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Euse appropriately sized specimens. As a minimum: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Emature trees \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould\u003C/strong\u003E be replaced with extra heavy standard trees \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Esemi-mature trees \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Ebe replaced with heavy standard trees \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EException:\u003C/strong\u003E Where removal of any Category A or B trees (as defined in Table 1 of British Standard (BS) 5837:2012) is unavoidable, their value should be assessed using the Capital Asset Value for Amenity Trees (CAVAT) method and appropriate mitigation clearly demonstrated within the proposed landscaping scheme.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
